      "field": "description",
      "fieldId": "description",
      "fieldtype": "jira",
      "from": null,
      "fromString": "h3. Description\n\nIn the Day view a planner can drag a job left or right to change what time it starts. It is meant to move in quarter-hour steps so a job can start at, say, quarter past eight. In practice the smallest move it will make is a whole hour, so anything that does not start on the hour cannot be set by dragging.\n\nh3. Branch / Environment\n\nBranch tested: https://sv8685.qa.shopview.com/schedule \u00b7 API host: https://sv8685api.qa.shopview.com \u00b7 Build marker (meta app-version): v3.5-4873abe \u00b7 index.html last-modified Tue, 04 Aug 2026 14:47:39 GMT, etag 9b4b1fc776ebbfb04a9a0ca051d847f7 \u00b7 Organisation d55bc308-e61a-438d-b5f1-c7a73c89d49f \u00b7 Location: Staging Heavy Duty - 9919 (b3c8c820-f815-4cf1-8938-10956c5ee71a, timezone America/Edmonton) \u00b7 Signed in as admin@shopview.com (Administrator) \u00b7 Observed 2026-08-04, 16:00-19:00 UTC.\n\nh3. Steps to reproduce\n\n# Open the Schedule and pick the Day view for Tuesday Aug 4, 2026.\n# Find any shift block on the grid - for example the Xiriver Apparel block, unit 16604, on Brittany Anderson's row.\n# Note the start time in the block's hover summary.\n# Press and hold the middle of the block and drag it a small distance to the right - about half of one hour column - then release.\n# Read the new start time in the hover summary.\n\nh3. Expected behaviour\n\nThe start time moves in quarter-hour steps, so a small drag moves it 15 or 30 minutes, and a job can be set to start at 8:15 or 8:45.\n\nh3. Current behaviour\n\nThe start time jumps a whole hour. A drag of about half an hour's width moved the job a full hour, and no quarter-hour position can be reached by dragging.\n\nh3. Images\n\nNo screenshot is attached. The evidence for this ticket is a captured DOM/state reading rather than a visual difference; the exact values are in the technical section below.\n\nh3. Technical details for developers\n\nA 24-pixel drag (approximately 31 minutes at the rendered zoom) issued PATCH /api/schedule/shifts/ebdd3e03-ab10-40f3-b820-4dd7e6192892 with startsAt '2026-08-04T14:00:00.000Z', i.e. exactly +60 minutes from 13:00:00Z. Spec section 4.8: 'Horizontal drag to move a shift's start time (snaps to 15-minute intervals).' Note this is a different surface from SV-8833, which is about the start/end pickers inside the shift window; both stem from 15-minute granularity not being applied, but the drag path and the picker path are separate. The shift moved during this test was put back to 13:00:00Z afterwards.",
      "to": null,
      "toString": "h3. Description\n\nIn the Day view a planner can drag a job left or right to change what time it starts. It is meant to move in quarter-hour steps so a job can start at, say, quarter past eight. In practice the smallest move it will make is a whole hour, so anything that does not start on the hour cannot be set by dragging.\n\nh3. Branch / Environment\n\nBranch tested: https://sv8685.qa.shopview.com/schedule \u00b7 API host: https://sv8685api.qa.shopview.com \u00b7 Build marker (meta app-version): v3.5-4873abe \u00b7 index.html last-modified Tue, 04 Aug 2026 14:47:39 GMT, etag 9b4b1fc776ebbfb04a9a0ca051d847f7 \u00b7 Organisation d55bc308-e61a-438d-b5f1-c7a73c89d49f \u00b7 Location: Staging Heavy Duty - 9919 (b3c8c820-f815-4cf1-8938-10956c5ee71a, timezone America/Edmonton) \u00b7 Signed in as admin@shopview.com (Administrator) \u00b7 Observed 2026-08-04, 16:00-19:00 UTC.\n\nh3. Steps to reproduce\n\n# Open the Schedule and pick the Day view for Tuesday Aug 4, 2026.\n# Find any shift block on the grid - for example the Xiriver Apparel block, unit 16604, on Brittany Anderson's row.\n# Note the start time in the block's hover summary.\n# Press and hold the middle of the block and drag it a small distance to the right - about half of one hour column - then release.\n# Read the new start time in the hover summary.\n\nh3. Expected behaviour\n\nThe start time moves in quarter-hour steps, so a small drag moves it 15 or 30 minutes, and a job can be set to start at 8:15 or 8:45.\n\nh3. Current behaviour\n\nThe start time jumps a whole hour. A drag of about half an hour's width moved the job a full hour, and no quarter-hour position can be reached by dragging.\n\nh3. Images\n\nNo screenshot is attached. The evidence for this ticket is a captured DOM/state reading rather than a visual difference; the exact values are in the technical section below.\n\nh3. Technical details for developers\n\nA 24-pixel drag (approximately 31 minutes at the rendered zoom) issued PATCH /api/schedule/shifts/ebdd3e03-ab10-40f3-b820-4dd7e6192892 with startsAt '2026-08-04T14:00:00.000Z', i.e. exactly +60 minutes from 13:00:00Z. Spec section 4.8: 'Horizontal drag to move a shift's start time (snaps to 15-minute intervals).' Note this is a different surface from SV-8833, which is about the start/end pickers inside the shift window; both stem from 15-minute granularity not being applied, but the drag path and the picker path are separate. The shift moved during this test was put back to 13:00:00Z afterwards.\n\n \n\nWhere this expected behaviour comes from: the Schedule specification, version 23, section 4.8 (Day view: timeline interactions), which says: \"Horizontal drag to move a shift's start time (snaps to 15-minute intervals).\""
     }
