  "description": "<h3><a name=\"Description\"></a>Description</h3>\n\n<p>In the Day view a planner can drag a job left or right to change what time it starts. It is meant to move in quarter-hour steps so a job can start at, say, quarter past eight. In practice the smallest move it will make is a whole hour, so anything that does not start on the hour cannot be set by dragging.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"Branch%2FEnvironment\"></a>Branch / Environment</h3>\n\n<p>Branch tested: <a href=\"https://sv8685.qa.shopview.com/schedule\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://sv8685.qa.shopview.com/schedule</a> \u00b7 API host: <a href=\"https://sv8685api.qa.shopview.com\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://sv8685api.qa.shopview.com</a> \u00b7 Build marker (meta app-version): v3.5-4873abe \u00b7 index.html last-modified Tue, 04 Aug 2026 14:47:39 GMT, etag 9b4b1fc776ebbfb04a9a0ca051d847f7 \u00b7 Organisation d55bc308-e61a-438d-b5f1-c7a73c89d49f \u00b7 Location: Staging Heavy Duty - 9919 (b3c8c820-f815-4cf1-8938-10956c5ee71a, timezone America/Edmonton) \u00b7 Signed in as admin@shopview.com (Administrator) \u00b7 Observed 2026-08-04, 16:00-19:00 UTC.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"Stepstoreproduce\"></a>Steps to reproduce</h3>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li>Open the Schedule and pick the Day view for Tuesday Aug 4, 2026.</li>\n\t<li>Find any shift block on the grid - for example the Xiriver Apparel block, unit 16604, on Brittany Anderson's row.</li>\n\t<li>Note the start time in the block's hover summary.</li>\n\t<li>Press and hold the middle of the block and drag it a small distance to the right - about half of one hour column - then release.</li>\n\t<li>Read the new start time in the hover summary.</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<h3><a name=\"Expectedbehaviour\"></a>Expected behaviour</h3>\n\n<p>The start time moves in quarter-hour steps, so a small drag moves it 15 or 30 minutes, and a job can be set to start at 8:15 or 8:45.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"Currentbehaviour\"></a>Current behaviour</h3>\n\n<p>The start time jumps a whole hour. A drag of about half an hour's width moved the job a full hour, and no quarter-hour position can be reached by dragging.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"Images\"></a>Images</h3>\n\n<p>No screenshot is attached. The evidence for this ticket is a captured DOM/state reading rather than a visual difference; the exact values are in the technical section below.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"Technicaldetailsfordevelopers\"></a>Technical details for developers</h3>\n\n<p>A 24-pixel drag (approximately 31 minutes at the rendered zoom) issued PATCH /api/schedule/shifts/ebdd3e03-ab10-40f3-b820-4dd7e6192892 with startsAt '2026-08-04T14:00:00.000Z', i.e. exactly +60 minutes from 13:00:00Z. Spec section 4.8: 'Horizontal drag to move a shift's start time (snaps to 15-minute intervals).' Note this is a different surface from \n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro\" data-jira-key=\"SV-8833\" >\n                <a href=\"https://shopview.atlassian.net/browse/SV-8833\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\"  title=\"Shift time picker allows any minute instead of 15-minute increments\" >\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10854?size=medium\" />\n            SV-8833\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-complete jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Ready to Fix</span>\n            </span>\n, which is about the start/end pickers inside the shift window; both stem from 15-minute granularity not being applied, but the drag path and the picker path are separate. The shift moved during this test was put back to 13:00:00Z afterwards.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Where this expected behaviour comes from: the Schedule specification, version 23, section 4.8 (Day view: timeline interactions), which says: \"Horizontal drag to move a shift's start time (snaps to 15-minute intervals).\"</p>",
